# NoiseModelling Benchmark

Compares several NoiseModelling versions on the same dataset (Clisson, France) and publishes the results as a
static website on GitHub Pages: <https://universite-gustave-eiffel.github.io/NoiseModellingBenchmark/>

## Where is what

| Path | What it does |
|---|---|
| `versions.json` | the list of versions to compare: `version -> release zip URL`. An **empty URL** marks the "head" version, taken from the NoiseModelling CI binary |
| `benchmark_run.sh` | the driver: download the binary, run the simulation, aggregate the results |
| `compare_versions.py` | builds the pairwise comparisons (`comparisons.json`) |
| `generate_site.py` | builds `website/index.html` from `website/template.html` and the JSON files |
| `website/template.html` | the page structure (HTML only) |
| `website/app.js` | all the page JavaScript |
| `website/index.css` | all the page CSS |
| `website/data/` | **generated, not in git**: `results.json`, `comparisons.json`, `settings.json`, `build.json`, and one folder of map layers per version |
| `nm_version/src/main/groovy/` | the simulation scripts launched by NoiseModelling: `runscriptV5.0.groovy`, `runscriptV6.0.groovy`, plus one script per version when the API changed |
| `input/clisson/` | the reference dataset (Git LFS) |
| `.github/workflows/benchmark.yml` | the CI: one job matrix per Java version, the "head" job, the website build, the Pages deploy |
| `LICENSE` | GPL-3.0 |

## How it works

1. `benchmark_run.sh --version v5.0.1` downloads that release, then NoiseModelling's ScriptRunner runs
   `nm_version/src/main/groovy/runscriptV5.0.groovy` on `input/clisson/`; results land in `output/v5.0.1/`.
2. `benchmark_run.sh --aggregate-only` turns `output/*/` into `website/data/` and computes the comparisons.
3. The CI does 1 and 2 for every version of `versions.json`, then publishes `website/` on GitHub Pages.

## Run it locally

```bash
bash benchmark_run.sh --version v5.0.1   # one version
bash benchmark_run.sh                    # every version of versions.json (skips the head)
bash benchmark_run.sh --aggregate-only   # only rebuild the site from output/
```

Needs Python 3, git-lfs (for `input/clisson/`) and Java 11 for v4/v5 or Java 25 for v6.
The NoiseModelling binary is downloaded automatically from the release URL in `versions.json`.

## Rules that keep the results comparable

- A version runs with **Java 25** when its name starts with `v6`, with **Java 11** otherwise.
- Levels ≤ **-89 dB** are treated as `NaN`: excluded from means, histograms and comparisons (they appear as a
  `NaN` column in the histogram).
- Keep **one single entry without URL** in `versions.json`: it is the "head" version, built by the
  NoiseModelling CI (on a fork this needs the optional `GH_PAT` secret).
- Do not modify `input/clisson/`: published results would no longer be comparable.
